Root cause:
The bug was caused by invoking the NAPI variant of the function `xdp_return_frame_rx_napi()` in a context where it was not allowed, specifically during the teardown of a CPU map entry. The teardown code was not running in the RX NAPI context, leading to potential synchronization issues and incorrect handling of XDP frames. This was particularly problematic when the `bq_flush_to_queue` function was called without the proper context, resulting in frames being returned incorrectly and potentially causing instability in the system.
